 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "b1fb4b20-223a-5224-b15e-06a76416065c"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11983/ma-source-field/cbf012bfd393c7a7a396b66ce0f9ac3343be277c252007b0c7c654ba2cd71624"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
