 {:db/id "q-12043" :question/id #uuid "0591c45f-50ff-5065-b712-d7946fc4e140" :question/math-academy-id "q-12043" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=12.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12043/ma-source-field/44050165b3f2b92dc602e3bb69796f55d7f77187f639e84b6053fa5330e8ee36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
