 {:db/id "q-12549" :question/id #uuid "d5829032-59a0-5111-b1d8-47c7a5a05911" :question/math-academy-id "q-12549" :question/problem "Given $P(A)=0.25$, $P(B)=0.75$, $P(A\\cup B)=0.8$, determine whether  $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events." :question/worked-solution "To check if $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive, we must check that $P(A\\cap B)=0.$\n\nWe can calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.25+0.75-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.75-0.8 \\\\  & =0.2\\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ and $B$ are not mutually exclusive events." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12549/ma-source-field/99d6d0ee8edba10392f436a3c5df138e10a745314cb4e9beb70459ef8320378d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
