 {:db/id "q-13635" :question/id #uuid "0dc1caab-e8b2-5f4c-af54-cbacb852a075" :question/math-academy-id "q-13635" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 1 & (-3)\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-13635/ma-source-field/3160429b3be2a367988476806808665b09625aaa793391ed25ea3231f455621a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
