 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d6f9badf-44cd-56b4-946a-abae3220a5b7"] :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-13759/ma-source-field/1d168f635b32e79b9aff435244ae0722254b7edf513db268b8988b493a9a9d37"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
