 {:db/id "q-13781" :question/id #uuid "ce57af24-7688-5285-99c2-a982d174d89c" :question/math-academy-id "q-13781" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=4\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-13781/ma-source-field/e026f89690e4a0c5be8ca89a3af0f624736a683e5a6961026ca63773446255dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
