 {:db/id "q-15460" :question/id #uuid "bf1d8b4a-8091-5076-a3c1-f3d77fa5e29a" :question/math-academy-id "q-15460" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}=55+10y.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2} & =55+10y \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =55 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =55+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,5)$ and its radius is $9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15460/ma-source-field/84a1c76a691f8c71b6aac935c671fb771263a89ba4939e8ba1162e891f1d72d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
