 {:db/id "q-8054" :question/id #uuid "3ddcb294-a508-54d0-bd15-63145db8f082" :question/math-academy-id "q-8054" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=3.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8054/ma-source-field/53c7ddf8ddc00b934ee89e0216bf262db4f3527c9c107dac538ec3d7bd02e0ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
