 {:db/id "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "4259dafc-1a37-55ff-aa39-09cc98e980bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/02684cbc3cb9cf19534614add5c44dcac0f8c90699569d5cb05d9b21dc74178b" "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/354549e05d30f5acb6c9a5e876a1b220679b1daee3381277145bd16fe273c514" "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/83351679bef40cdde3e69e55c2c6f08222a317ed82557f1e3ec0abdce5a513f4" "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/7fa603eaeff54701c0d44670b8ee09b596de6f8708827eb6deb18e39238c5ef7" "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/6913df9b151f2261420536f52f0de81cdd0d2e27ea8c5c83cbd8846242d77d1b"] :answer-field/correct "q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca/7fa603eaeff54701c0d44670b8ee09b596de6f8708827eb6deb18e39238c5ef7" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-8060" :question/id #uuid "e53a5dab-4c76-5167-b8bb-303aab059a57" :question/math-academy-id "q-8060" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection in the line $y=-x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8060/ma-source-field/c6c4c324748e06fe987c447f41f75ad83ea6187e934622856ecd610f920418ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
