 {:db/id "q-9347" :question/id #uuid "33ca03a0-a8c8-587c-a9fa-20692dfe790c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9347" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(D-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 9-3\\lambda -3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =5,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-9347/ma-source-field/54347bbd4acf6ba7675f27909bbf3499ff8505bf9bc63c91c0d2cd867bac1c49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
